+# Multi‑party cosign approvals (guidance)
+
+Goal: require N-of-M cosign sign‑blob approvals before certain high‑impact actions (e.g., production promotion, dataset purge).
+
+1. Set up a KMS key for cosign and restrict usage to the approver service principal(s).
+2. Each approver obtains a short-lived credential / OIDC token mapped to a KMS grant or signs via a dedicated approver mediator.
+3. To sign a blob:
+   cosign sign-blob --key awskms://arn:aws:kms:... approver_payload.bin
+4. Use Rekor to record signatures for audit:
+   rekor-cli upload --artifact approver_payload.bin --signature approver_payload.bin.sig --public-key <pub>
+5. Verification:
+   cosign verify-blob --key awskms://... --signature approver_payload.bin.sig approver_payload.bin
+6. Orchestrator checks that required N signatures exist before executing high-risk Argo templates.
